# The catalog the APK ships, cooked on the build host and extracted on first launch.
#
# `Any` rather than WindowsX64: this catalog is consumed on a device, and a cooked
# object records its target platform in the header. Nothing in the cooker branches on
# the value and no loader validates it beyond "is it a known enum", so naming a desktop
# platform here would be a lie that happens to work. `Any` is the honest description of
# a catalog whose objects are byte-identical everywhere -- which these are, because the
# only formats used are uncompressed RGBA8 and a UV rect.
platform Any

# A 2x2 inline texture, RRGGBBAA left to right then top to bottom. Inline so this file
# needs no image on disk, which is what lets the Android cook run from a clean checkout.
#
# The four corners are deliberately different colours: a device screenshot can then tell
# "the catalog loaded and the sampler is right" from "something drew a flat quad".
texture2d 0100000000000000000000000000001a 2 2 FFFFFFFF FF4C4CFF 4CFF4CFF 4C4CFFFF

# A sprite covering the whole texture. Present so the catalog carries a dependency edge:
# a single standalone asset would load even if dependency resolution were broken.
sprite 0200000000000000000000000000002a 0100000000000000000000000000001a 0 0 1 1 0.5 0.5 32
